	<description>
		'This task is a standard reach-out task, reaching from a center target to a peripheral one.  But there is a visuomotor rotation that is applied.  In this protocol, it goes from 0 to 45 degrees in 5 degree increments per trial (i.e. very fast).  It then stays at 45d for 8 trials followed a single catch trial in which the rotation disappears.'
	</description>
